                <pb facs="0815" n="727" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg727"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Translation of a memorandum left with the Secretary of
                        State by the Russian ambassador March 28, 1904.</hi></head>
                <p>Japan having openly violated the neutrality of Korea and usurped the power in
                    that country, which has from this fact become the theater of the hostilities,
                    Russia, for her part, finds herself constrained to adopt such measures as the
                    circumstances demand, and deems it her duty to warn all neutral powers of the
                    danger in which vessels calling at Korean ports may be involved through the
                    present development of the war.</p>
            </div>
